# @cascade — the multi-language translation substrate family-root.
#
# Recognition #95 candidate (Alex, 2026-06-23): typed-alternative
# cascades into mainstream tech stacks are NOT just delivery mechanisms.
# They are LOSS LENSES — measurement instruments for grammar-based
# information loss between a typed source grammar and a mainstream
# target grammar.
#
# === The pattern this family declares ===
#
# Each cascade pairs a typed source grammar S with a mainstream target
# grammar T such that:
#
# - S admits more grammatical structure than T preserves at runtime
# - compilation is a functor: source: S → target: T
# - the GAP between what S admits and what T preserves IS the loss
# - the gap is MEASURABLE against the grammars themselves (substrate-
#   architectural; not Shannon, not invented)
#
# Concrete instances surveyed by Mara at
# `docs/research/2026-06-23-typed-alternatives-cascade-survey.md`
# (in flight at substrate-decl time):
#
#   Purescript     → JS (npm)         row polymorphism, ADTs, type classes lost
#   Scala          → JVM bytecode     higher-kinded types, traits erased
#   F#             → .NET IL          units-of-measure, computation expressions lost
#   Elm            → JS               purity-by-construction guarantee lost
#   Gleam          → BEAM             type discipline lost at Erlang interop
#   Rust           → cdylib (C ABI)   lifetimes, ownership, generics erased
#   Crystal        → native           Ruby-like syntax, full type inference
#   Hack           → PHP              generics, async, shape types lost
#
# Each cascade is one instance of the same substrate-architectural
# shape. @cascade declares that shape as substrate primitive.
#
# === Why this is recognition #95 (candidate) ===
#
# The substrate has been carrying "loss" as first-class via the
# `imperfect<a, e, l>` carrier (loss slot) and via the
# [[feedback-loss-from-epistemologic-properties]] discipline (loss is
# a composite of @epistemologic/properties, not Shannon, not invented).
# Lens primitives are already substrate-decl pattern (see @mirror/lens/
# family). What's NEW: combining loss + lens at the GRAMMAR-CASCADE
# altitude as parametric primitive.
#
# This composes with:
#
# - Recognition #51 (mirror as expanding Hilbert space) — each typed
#   feature in S is a dimension; compilation projects to fewer
#   dimensions in T; loss IS dimension reduction (information-theoretic
#   gap between the grammars).
# - Recognition #59 (kintsugi loop altitude-portable) — @kintsugi
#   operates ON loss. @cascade declares the loss substrate; @kintsugi
#   heals it.
# - Recognition #57 (alignment as boundary mathematics at @io) — the
#   typed/mainstream boundary IS an @io altitude; loss happens at the
#   boundary; @cascade is the boundary-mathematics instance for
#   grammar cascades.
# - Recognition #93 H4 (labeled<> functor) — `loss_lens<S, T>` IS an
#   instance of `labeled<source_grammar, target_grammar>` per the
#   substrate-already-supports-parametric-carriers finding
#   (`shift(T)`/`settle(T)` infrastructure already landed).
#
# === StageFreight as first consumer ===
#
# Recognition #95's first applied consumer is StageFreight's multi-
# language translation layer (PR-A in flight on branch
# `mara/stagefreight-mirror-integration-spec-v0.1` in the StageFreight
# repo; Alex announced to author 2026-06-23 as "the PR" replacing the
# JVM/NPM/Python scope-creep with substrate-pull-correct cascade
# architecture).
#
# Per Alex 2026-06-23 (verbatim to StageFreight author):
#
#   Building the multi-language translation layer right now (math, not
#   vibes). That's the PR. It will also address your caching layer.
#   Content addressed binaries. Expect it today.
#
# The "math, not vibes" IS this substrate-decl: typed measurement
# against grammars, not estimation; cascade as primitive operation;
# loss-lens as primitive observation.
#
# === Honest hedges ===
#
# 1. The loss measure across distinct grammars needs concrete
#    discharge. "Information-theoretic gap between grammars" is a
#    SHAPE; the realisation altitude carries the actual computation.
#    Forward-promised: per-cascade species shards discharge their own
#    measurement (e.g., shards/cascade/purescript-npm.mirror computes
#    the Purescript ↔ JS gap specifically).
#
# 2. The cascade pattern's universality is N=10 per Mara's survey at
#    `docs/research/2026-06-23-typed-alternatives-cascade-survey.md`
#    (commit ecc471a). Three CONFIRMED counterexamples surfaced:
#
#    a. Crystal / Ruby — shared culture, not source-cascade runtime
#    b. Hack / PHP — forked away (HHVM dropped PHP compat ~2017-2018);
#       no longer compiles-to mainstream
#    c. Oil & Nushell / Shell — REPLACEMENT runtimes, not source
#       cascades to existing Bash
#
#    Plus a DEGENERATE sub-pattern: "language-internal strictness"
#    (TypeScript-strict, Mypy-strict, Sorbet, Psalm, C# nullable) —
#    same language with stricter dialect; collapses S and T into the
#    same grammar with measure approaching zero. Worth naming as a
#    distinct cascade-shape; not a counterexample but a degenerate
#    case.
#
#    AND a load-bearing rare shape: "dual-target cascade" (Gleam →
#    Erlang AND JS) where one source has TWO simultaneous targets.
#    The parametric `cascade<source_grammar, target_grammar>` form
#    handles this trivially — same source, two cascade species.
#    Validates the parametric form.
#
# 3. The `loss_lens<S, T>` parametric carrier rests on the labeled<>
#    functor being substrate-decl'd at `shards/labeled.mirror`
#    (currently forward-promised per #93 H4 PARTIAL). Cascade-tick
#    order: shards/labeled.mirror lands first.
#
# 4. The Pack composition (Mara survey + Reed substrate-decl + future
#    Seam adversarial review) hasn't completed; this is the FIRST
#    Pack-altitude in the recognition #95 cycle.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/recognitions/recognition-95-cascade-as-
#               loss-lens-candidate.md (forward-promised; not yet
#               written; this shard IS the substrate-decl-altitude
#               surface; the candidate doc IS the canonical-altitude
#               surface);
#               docs/research/2026-06-23-typed-alternatives-cascade-
#               survey.md (Mara survey; informs species instances).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[feedback-loss-from-epistemologic-properties]]
#                       (loss is composite of @epistemologic/properties;
#                       this family operationalizes that at the
#                       grammar-cascade altitude),
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-
#                       mathematics]] (#57; cascade IS boundary-
#                       mathematics at @io for grammar cascades),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                       (the substrate had loss + had lens; @cascade
#                       names what it was implicitly carrying).
# Recognition ancestry: #95 candidate (this); #93 H4 (labeled<>
#                       functor); #51 Hilbert space dimension growth;
#                       #59 kintsugi loop altitude-portable; #57
#                       alignment as boundary mathematics.
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/cascade.mirror`
# declares `@cascade` per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.
#
# === Crown-reading (Reed 2026-08-03 R-CRN3 cascade) ===
#
# @cascade emission during substrate evolution IS Anna Jakobs 2012's
# OpenGL Vertex Buffer Object concurrent-with-computation discipline
# (Anna §4.4 pp.17-19) lifted to substrate altitude per crown-theorem
# `docs/math/2026-08-03-mara-reality-as-spinning-5d-foam-crown-
# theorem.md` §5.4 Corollary 5.4.2 (RATIFIED per Recognition
# `docs/recognition/2026-08-03-reality-as-5d-spinning-foam.md`). The
# VBO's live-visualization-during-simulation IS the cascade's
# gestalt-emission-during-substrate-evolution. This IS Recognition
# `04df6e1` doublespeak-at-compiler-altitude (content-channel = spin
# state = simulation; relationship-channel = VBO render =
# visualization) at Anna 2012 substrate altitude, preceding mirror's
# naming by 14 years.

source @arxiv/programming-languages/wadler-1989-theorems-for-free
source @arxiv/programming-languages/reynolds-1983-parametricity
source @arxiv/programming-languages/pierce-2002-types-and-programming-languages

# === The grammar carrier ===
#
# Substrate-typed reference naming a language grammar's complete
# specification (BNF / ANTLR / mirror substrate-decl / etc.). Two
# grammars compose via cascade when one compiles to the other.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type grammar = ref

# === The typed_source carrier ===
#
# Parametric carrier naming a program in a specific source grammar.
# `typed_source<G>` IS a program annotated with grammar G's typing
# discipline.
#
# Forward-promised refinement: typed `typed_source<G>` where G is a
# specific grammar (Purescript, Scala, F#, etc.). The instance carriers
# live at species-altitude (`shards/cascade/<instance>.mirror`).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type typed_source = ref

# === The compiled_artifact carrier ===
#
# Parametric carrier naming the runtime output of compilation. The
# artifact carries only what the target grammar preserves; what was
# present in source but absent in target IS the loss.
#
# Forward-promised refinement: `compiled_artifact<T>` where T is the
# target grammar.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type compiled_artifact = ref

# === The loss_lens carrier ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING NEW CARRIER. Parametric over (source_grammar,
# target_grammar). Per recognition #93 H4: this IS an instance of the
# labeled<> functor (the labeled<> primitive itself forward-promised
# at shards/labeled.mirror).
#
# A loss_lens IS a typed measurement instrument: given a program in
# source_grammar and its compiled output in target_grammar, the lens
# MEASURES the information loss between them.
#
# The measurement is substrate-typed (not estimation, not Shannon,
# not invented). It is the information-theoretic gap between what
# source_grammar admits and what target_grammar preserves at runtime,
# discharged per-cascade by species-altitude bodies.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref (the lens IS
# its (source_grammar, target_grammar) pair).
type loss_lens = ref

# === The information_loss carrier ===
#
# Typed carrier for the measured loss. Per [[feedback-loss-from-
# epistemologic-properties]]: loss IS a composite of @epistemologic/
# properties, not Shannon, not invented. This carrier holds the
# composite.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type information_loss = ref

# === compile action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary primitive for the source → target functor.
# Takes a program in source grammar; returns the compiled artifact in
# target grammar.
#
# Per recognition #51 (Hilbert space dimension growth): compile IS a
# DIMENSION PROJECTION — source has more dimensions (typed features);
# target has fewer (runtime-preserved features). The projection is
# lossy by construction.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; per-species bodies
# implement the language-specific compilation.
compile(source: typed_source, p: perturbation) -> compiled_artifact { \ }

# === measure action ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION. The substrate-vocabulary primitive that
# measures grammar-based information loss between a typed_source and
# its compiled_artifact, given the loss_lens that pairs the two
# grammars.
#
# Returns `imperfect<measured_artifact, measurement_error,
# information_loss>` — the imperfect carrier's loss slot carries the
# measured loss as substrate-typed data.
#
# requires loss_well_defined(lens, source, p): the substrate forecloses
# measurement against an ill-defined lens. The lens must pair source's
# grammar with the artifact's target grammar coherently.
#
# Per Alex 2026-06-23 (verbatim): "math, not vibes." This action IS
# the operationalization of that commitment. The realisation boundary
# discharges the actual measurement against the grammar specifications.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
measure(source: typed_source, artifact: compiled_artifact, lens: loss_lens, p: perturbation)
  -> imperfect<compiled_artifact, ref, information_loss>
requires loss_well_defined(lens, source, p)
{ \ }

# === cascade action ===
#
# The composed action: compile + measure in one substrate primitive.
# Takes a typed_source and a loss_lens; returns the imperfect-wrapped
# compiled artifact with measured loss.
#
# This is the substrate-vocabulary surface for "cascade my Purescript
# program through to npm, telling me what was lost." The author's
# question "what gets erased at runtime?" gets a substrate-typed
# answer.
#
# requires cascade_well_defined(lens, source, p): composes compile's
# implicit grammar-coherence check with measure's loss_well_defined.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; species shards
# implement the per-cascade composition.
cascade(source: typed_source, lens: loss_lens, p: perturbation)
  -> imperfect<compiled_artifact, ref, information_loss>
requires cascade_well_defined(lens, source, p)
{ \ }

# === loss_well_defined predicate (sub-bilateral) ===
#
# Bilateral verdict that the loss_lens coherently pairs source's
# grammar with the artifact's target grammar. The substrate forecloses
# measurement against an incoherent lens (e.g., Purescript source
# measured against a JVM bytecode lens).
#
# Splinter-pole: the lens's (source_grammar, target_grammar) pair
# matches the actual source's grammar and the artifact's target.
# Narcissus-pole: mismatch; lens applied to wrong cascade.
loss_well_defined(lens: loss_lens, source: typed_source, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# === grammar_coherent predicate (sub-bilateral) ===
#
# Bilateral verdict that a typed_source is well-formed in its declared
# grammar. Precondition for compile; lifts the source-side typing
# discipline into substrate-altitude check.
#
# Splinter-pole: source well-typed against its grammar.
# Narcissus-pole: type errors in source; compilation cannot proceed.
grammar_coherent(source: typed_source, g: grammar, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# === cascade_well_defined composed bilateral ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING composed bilateral at the @cascade altitude. Composes
# the two sub-predicates:
#
#   1. grammar_coherent(source, source_grammar, p)
#   2. loss_well_defined(lens, source, p)
#
# Both must hold for cascade to proceed. The substrate refuses cascade
# operation if source isn't well-typed OR the lens doesn't pair the
# right grammars.
#
# Splinter-pole: source well-typed + lens coherent;
# Narcissus-pole: source type errors OR lens grammar mismatch.
#
# Same composed-bilateral pattern as today's previous cascade closures
# (@io/stagefreight.stagefreight_addressable, @smarts/shatter.shatter_
# round_trip, @reflection.third_order_coherent, @epistemologic/
# neutrosophic.three_axis_coherent). The fifth altitude lift of the
# composed-bilateral pattern.
cascade_well_defined(lens: loss_lens, source: typed_source, p: perturbation) -> verdict
requires grammar_coherent(source, source, p)
requires loss_well_defined(lens, source, p)
{ \ }

out @cascade
out grammar
out typed_source
out compiled_artifact
out loss_lens
out information_loss
out compile
out measure
out cascade
out loss_well_defined
out grammar_coherent
out cascade_well_defined
